# p_5f9b — Home-based couple; evening wind-down moves objects to bedrooms and storage after 21:00

A fresh document for a routine the library lacks: the evening-to-night migration. Every existing document models the waking day (roughly 7:00-21:00) but leaves the 21:00-24:00 and 00:00-04:00 windows to fall-through statistics. The mixture's worst-objects list is dominated by 22:00 and 00:00 sightings where objects are at receptacles no daytime block predicts: object_15 at receptacle_19 (2x at 22:00), object_19 at receptacle_8, object_21 at receptacle_8, object_17 at receptacle_15, object_5 at receptacle_19, object_23 at receptacle_21, object_25 at receptacle_21 (all at 22:00), and object_12 at receptacle_22, object_32 at receptacle_22, object_10 at receptacle_17 (all at 00:00).

The hypothesis: after the couple finishes their work and dinner (around 21:00), they do a "tidy-up" pass. Kitchen items go back to shelves (object_15 → receptacle_19). Desk and living-room items get put away in bedrooms or storage (object_19, object_21 → receptacle_8, which is a bedroom shelf; object_17 → receptacle_15, another storage area). Personal items that were out during the day return to their rooms (object_23, object_25 → receptacle_21, a bedroom or closet). By midnight, the house is in "sleep mode": bathroom-area items (object_12, object_32) are at receptacle_22 (a bathroom shelf or cabinet), and the side-shelf item object_10 has been moved to receptacle_17 (a different storage spot).

The couple is home-based (object_2, object_35 always at receptacle_11; object_3 at receptacle_7). Nothing leaves the house. The daytime routine is standard: object_4 at receptacle_18, object_15/16 at receptacle_4, object_14 at receptacle_12, object_13 at receptacle_6. What this document adds is the 21:00-24:00 and 00:00-04:00 blocks.

